## Visual concept

The **Calibration Bench / zeroing station** — the metrology pass before first power-up, continuing the PE arc from 1.0's commissioning console (this poster = key K4 expanded). Hero is a **zeroing gauge**: the factory reference band ghosted/printed on the dial (`LAB REFERENCE RANGE — population average · NOT YOU`) versus a freshly-struck green personal zero (`YOUR ZERO — set while healthy`), with zero-adjust screw, law plate (`YOU CANNOT MANAGE WHAT YOU HAVE NEVER MEASURED.`) and three output chips (dealbreakers→1.0 NO-GO tie-line / your reference point / fertility captured→Zone 5). Then: a five-tag **chain-of-custody prep strip** (hydrate / fast / draw 07:00–10:00 / hold training / abstain) ending in the amber false-E2 fault chip ("bad prep doesn't just lie — it prescribes"); a six-bay **instrument rack** with one headline marker per bay (HEMATOCRIT + amber respect plate >52–54%, HDL+ApoB, CYSTATIN-C, GGT, the wider/brighter HORMONES bay, SUPPORT) with the **compensated sensor pairs** inset docked to bays 3–4 (muscle/training injects into creatinine·AST/ALT raw channels flagged `READS FALSELY STRESSED`, corrected green channels cystatin-C·GGT, decoder line); a **growth-signal interlock** (gate held open only by a completed cancer-marker sweep, 3×3 organ-map grid, cadence pills, pituitary fine print); the sealed **archival vault** (semen analysis, rotated `NON-RETAKEABLE` tag, green `IF NORMAL: FREEZE.`); and the **inspection timetable** (home always-on chips + four blood checkpoints with mid-cycle emphasized, angled amber inspection stamp `EVERY 6–12 MONTHS = MONITORING IN NAME ONLY.`). Malaysia rail runs full-height right as a priced parts list (P·01–P·05, home BP cuff boxed as highest-value).

Semantic color rationed per brief §5: success green = personal zero, prep ticks, corrected channels, FREEZE; warning amber = respect plate, jammed channels, fault chip, NON-RETAKEABLE, inspection stamp; danger red = exactly TWO objects (growth-signal physics plate, invisible-disasters plate). Locked Fit "Engineering Diagnostic Instrument" style, palette matched to PE 1.0 (#000 ground, #141417 modules, #34D399/#F59E0B/#EF4444 states, Inter display + mono labels).

